cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. All outputs are SYNTHETIC; this is an independent research prototype, not a medical device."
title: "Spark OES-512 BioSignal Explorer: an independent prototype for explainable 512-channel biosignal monitoring in the browser"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/spark-oes512-demo"
url: "https://sparkainlp-x.github.io/spark-oes512-demo/"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
abstract: >-
  Single self-contained HTML page (no external resources, no backend, no AI
  API). A synthetic 512-channel frame is split into 16 blocks of 32; each
  block is scored with S = 0.45·max|x| + 0.35·RMS + 0.20·mean|x| and alerts
  when S ≥ threshold (default 0.50, adjustable). Missing data (NaN) triggers
  human review and is never scored. Seeded deterministic scenarios, an
  explainability panel, JSON export, CSV import, a rule-based plain-English
  explainer and an in-page self-test. Synthetic data only.
  Not a medical device, not diagnostic, not clinically validated.
keywords:
  - explainable monitoring
  - biosignal
  - block score
  - oes512
  - human review
  - synthetic data
